### G-ASAN: AddressSanitizer over the workspace test suites (Linux/aarch64) ###
feature lane: rustty-vt:wuffs,oniguruma — the PNG decode tests (`image_load_png_zlib_compressed_direct`, `sys::tests::default_decoder_*`) are ignored without the wuffs feature, and one of them is a Miri exception whose stated compensating control is ASan; found by G-ASAN's claim cross-check on its first run (P7-W14); and the oniguruma feature's tests, e.g. the Miri-excepted tmux::control::concurrent_first_notifications_do_not_race_oniguruma_init, which no lane compiled until the cross-check covered every Miri exception (fix round 1)
feature lane: rustty-apprt:gtk,wayland,x11 — GTK is the reference's Linux runtime, so its test executable there compiles the GTK apprt; cargo test --workspace does not
feature lane: rustty-os:flatpak — the Flatpak arm of rustty-os (links gio-2.0, Linux/FreeBSD only); cargo test --workspace does not build it
